    "body": "Reverse relation values can be present in memory while a shape-only selector includes introductory words. Extend the existing signed-H4 start learner with bounded exact lexical/prime context and ordered occurrence pairs. A construction-prompt registry counts recurrence across distinct owners selected by the frozen parent writer, reducing payload memorization. Parent parameters, candidate admission, endpoints, payloads and immutable versions remain fixed. The optional registry preserves older artifacts; the no-refit control keeps the lookup population and replaces only contextual roots with identity.\n\nRetain `50dc0d23` at bounded contextual phrase-start scope: 50/50 supported construction, 12/12 open development, 8/8 earlier start challenges and 12/12 fresh answers after selection and source eviction. Parent scores 12/50 and 3/12; the context-disabled control scores 38/50 and 7/12. All 663 retained construction answers and the selected forward/reverse, long-window, dependent, span and session preservation pass. Complete supplied construction remains 50/52: two upstream `quiet river` no-write cases are explicitly retained diagnostics. Open feedback informed new construction contrasts. The preparation stop, three rejected candidates and their source snapshots remain preserved. Four predecessor/first pair codes learn nonidentity roots; writer-role roots remain identity, with no isolated pair/role advantage claim.\n\nValidation executed locally:\n\n- Pinned, offline release builds of the native example, root CLI, core and allocation-test binaries.\n- Five relation-start tests, five relation-span tests, integer-kernel source guard and native architecture-policy check.\n- Actual-artifact malformed model rejection, exact parent/roundtrip, short/evicted outputs, per-step checkpoints and zero allocations during ingestion/emission.\n- Root CLI emits ` Cobalt Field.\\n` with EOS; the older shape-only artifact loads and preserves its opened ` Amber Meadow.\\n` case.\n- Formatting, claim-wording and diff-whitespace checks. Independent source/receipt review found no blocker.\n\nThis continuation used 483.207 model seconds and 1,280.628 engineering-command seconds. Cumulative model use is 4,870.743/4,950 seconds. Necessary extensions were recorded before use under standing owner authorization; all inherited charges, unique material and the 128 MiB storage stop margin are preserved. No external paid compute. Artifact loading was 14.65 seconds; the separate small input/emission samples establish no energy or broad efficiency advantage.\n\nThe result/evidence and current-state pointer record the next parent-preserving writer refinement, followed by shared transitions whose second operator consumes an actual first committed result. General phrase understanding, language/reasoning/coding, HTTP/WASM/Studio integration and energy remain unqualified. The five protected CI statuses are echo acknowledgements only; they execute no tests.\n\nReferences #1139, #1140 and #973. This partial delivery does not close their broader responsibilities.\n",
